# Android Plugin compileSdk Compatibility

## Mistake

Release build failed with `AAPT: error: resource android:attr/lStar not found`.

## Root Cause

A transitive Android library plugin used `compileSdkVersion 30`, while its AndroidX dependencies referenced API 31+ resources.

## Required Recipe

- In `android/build.gradle.kts`, enforce a minimum `compileSdk` for all Android library subprojects.
- Keep this guard in the shared `subprojects { afterEvaluate { ... } }` block so it applies to pub plugins too.
- Use a modern floor (`34` or current project compile SDK), never `< 31`.

```kotlin
subprojects {
    afterEvaluate {
        if (project.plugins.hasPlugin("com.android.library")) {
            extensions.configure<com.android.build.gradle.LibraryExtension> {
                if (compileSdk < 34) compileSdk = 34
            }
        }
    }
}
```

## Regression Check

- Run `fvm flutter build apk --release`.
- If it fails, inspect `build/.../values.xml` errors for missing `android:attr/*` resources and verify library module compile SDK values.
